{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR_isospin_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR_isospin_blind","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraneTowerIsospinBlind.lean#L55-L59","doc":"Isobar corollary of the collapse: the word-independent tower on two same-`A` isobars is\nidentical (the value is `∑_k C(3A−1,k) z^k f k`, with no word input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR_eq_binom_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR_eq_binom_sum","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraneTowerIsospinBlind.lean#L37-L53","doc":"**The trace-invariant tower collapses to a function of `(n, z, f)` only**:\n`braneTowerR n z f = ∑_{k ≤ n−1} C(n−1, k) z^k f k`. There is **no** braid-word input — this is\nthe algebraic content behind isospin-blindness (the value is fixed by the strand count `n = 3A`,\nso two isobars of the same `A` get the same tower). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerR","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraneTowerIsospinBlind.lean#L32-L35","doc":"The Markov-invariant (word-independent) R-side tower, weight `f` a function of subset size\nonly — the genuinely trace-invariant form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerW_isospin_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerW_isospin_blind","kind":"theorem","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraneTowerIsospinBlind.lean#L18-L30","doc":"**(b)-structural exclusion — isospin-blindness of the trace-invariant tower.**\nIf the per-subset weight is **Markov-invariant**, i.e. reduced-word independent\n(`w β₁ = w β₂` — the cited invariant `tr_M(σ_i) = z` is reduced-word independent), then two\nisobars `β₁, β₂` on the same `n = 3A` strands receive an **identical** brane-tower term. Hence\nthe contribution of the trace-invariant brane tower to the mirror-pair binding difference is\nexactly `0`: any mirror split must be carried by `T₁` (descended `tr_M`) and `T₅` (chirality),\nnot the brane tower. This prunes the search (synthesis\n`docs/audits/2026-06-26-t2t3-trace-invariance-status-synthesis.md`, owner-selected step 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraneTowerIsospinBlind.braneTowerW","kind":"def","line":11,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraneTowerIsospinBlind.lean#L11-L16","doc":"The R-side brane-tower term of a braid word `β` (drawn from an index type `ι`) on `n`\nstrands: a sum over subsets `S` of the `n − 1` adjacent generators of `z^{|S|}` times a\nper-subset weight `w β |S|`. The Markov-trace structure makes the weight depend on the subset\n*size* only (within a fixed word); `w β` lets it a-priori still depend on the word `β`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}